  "slug": "repair-abdominal-wall-ae98",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and papers add methylation error correction, single-cell methylome scaling, and reference-based deconvolution to epigenomic toolkits.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is improving the fidelity of epigenomic measurements through computational or chemical correction. Several items address DNA methylation specifically: HOMED applies hierarchical, reference-based deconvolution guided by cell-lineage hierarchies and scRNA-seq, JEEPERS detects and corrects jagged-end-induced methylation errors in cfDNA while preserving duplex integrity, and ctDNA-BERT scores individual bisulfite reads using CpG methylation, context, and fragment end, with AUC 0.884 for stage I. On the single-cell side, scEM-seq profiles tens of thousands of cells with reduced DNA loss and resolves immune lineages, while a Shannon entropy approach filters high-quality nuclei in scATAC-seq. Other items extend the scope to RNA editing (OmniRE-seq) and ambient-stable single-cell transcriptomics (Si-scRNA-seq). The new elements are read-level error correction for cfDNA methylation and transformer-based scoring of individual bisulfite reads.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
